    "statement": "On the F04 full-J chart, equality of the observed and expected product polynomials and nonvanishing of their constant factors imply equality of their logarithmic derivatives at W=0. Writing each observed factor as g=u^2-Wv^2 gives the exact contribution 2u1/u0-(v0/u0)^2, while the 24 expected linear factors give the corresponding reciprocal-label sum. After source simplification and symmetric c,d descent, the numerator is one irreducible degree-67 polynomial with 162322 terms. Its denominator has only named factors together with exactly two nonnamed degree-7 and two nonnamed degree-11 factors, each squared. Thus the full-J route splits exhaustively into four explicit denominator-zero branches and the guarded degree-67 numerator branch. No branch emptiness or literal-cell closure is claimed.",
